Package: nodedr-pos
Version: @VERSION@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: sqlite3
Suggests: xdg-utils, cups, printer-driver-escpr
Homepage: https://github.com/Raktim94/nodedr-pos
Description: Offline point-of-sale and inventory management system
 NodeDR POS is a self-contained point-of-sale and inventory system for small
 retail shops. It runs entirely on the local machine with no cloud service,
 no subscription and no internet connection after installation.
 .
 Features include barcode-scanner checkout, per-product GST with HSN codes and
 CGST/SGST split, percentage and flat discounts, a points loyalty programme,
 customer accounts with dues and store credit, multi-currency support, admin
 and cashier roles, sales history, an analytics dashboard, EAN-13/QR label
 generation, and CSV import for HSN/SAC, PIN code and IFSC reference data.
 .
 Receipts can be printed through the browser, downloaded as PDF, or sent
 directly to a USB ESC/POS thermal printer (58mm/80mm).
 .
 This package installs the application as a systemd service that starts at
 boot. The shop interface is served on http://localhost:1994 and is reachable
 from any tablet or phone on the same network. The API is bound to loopback
 only. All data is stored in a local SQLite database under
 /var/lib/nodedr-pos, which is preserved across upgrades and on removal, and
 deleted only on purge.
